course: dictionary
lesson: 490
title: Feeling ashamed: the word and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ashamed means feeling bad and guilty because you did something wrong, or feeling embarrassed about something. In «Ollie felt ashamed and scared that someone would come round and see», the words scared and hiding tell you he had done something he wanted to keep secret.
explain: Feeling ashamed after a mistake can help us say sorry and do better. But nobody should be made ashamed of who they are, such as their family, their skin, or their accent. «A food bank is a place that gives free food to people who need it; it is nothing to be ashamed of.» The clue is the words that come after: nothing to be ashamed of means there is no reason to feel bad.
explain: Ashamed is often followed by of or to: ashamed of, ashamed to. To check your meaning, swap in a word like guilty or embarrassed. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Ashamed is an adjective. Its forms are more ashamed and most ashamed.
fact: «Ashamed» means feeling bad and guilty because you did something wrong.
fact: «Ashamed of» someone means feeling that their behaviour reflects badly on you.
fact: «Nothing to be ashamed of» means there is no reason to feel bad.
fact: Ashamed is often used with feel: «She feels ashamed».
exercise: «Ollie felt ashamed and scared that someone would come round and see.» What does ashamed mean here? | Happy and excited to show his console | Feeling cold and tired | *Feeling bad about something he had done and hidden | Feeling proud of his old console
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means there is no reason to feel bad. | when money runs short | free food | a place | *nothing to be ashamed of
exercise: Which small word most often comes after ashamed in the lessons? | the | *of | sink | run
test: Should anyone be made ashamed of their family, skin or accent? | Only if they live in a big house | *No, nobody should be made ashamed of who they are | Only if they are very tall | Yes, always
test: Which sentence shows feeling ashamed after a mistake can help us say sorry? | Ben ran to the shop for milk | Sam laughed at the joke and went home | *Maya broke the vase, felt ashamed, said sorry and promised to be more careful | Jo watched the rain fall all afternoon
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to ashamed when someone has done something wrong? | *Guilty | Bored | Proud | Happy
